---
description: Best practices for NestJS 11 (TS 5.9, ESLint 8, Jest 30)
globs: */backend/src/**/*.ts,*/backend/test/**/*.ts
---

- Use modules/providers/controllers pattern; keep services stateless where possible
- DTOs with `class-validator` and `class-transformer`; validate incoming payloads
- Config via `@nestjs/config`; load env schema and validate
- TypeORM: use data mappers/repositories; handle transactions at service layer
- RxJS 7.8: use Observables only where needed; prefer async/await for I/O
- Swagger: decorate DTOs and endpoints for API documentation
- Health/Throttling: enable `@nestjs/terminus` and `@nestjs/throttler` when applicable
- Testing: Jest 30, unit tests for services/controllers; e2e tests under `test/`
- Lint/Format: ESLint 8 + Prettier 3; consistent import order and no unused vars

